2.27.e:
Then birth’s destruction he attained;
special knowledges perfected;
a sage with the three knowledges,
that brahmin’s a triple-knower.

2.28.e:
"Nanda, Rahula and Bhadda;
likewise the two chief followers;
Suddhodana Maharaja,
and Gotamī Pajāpatī;

Transmigrating in existence,
if I have ever disturbed you,
I’m announcing it, Great Hero;
please forgive my imperfection.

Body big as the universe,
she made the continent up north
her head; eastern, western her wings;
and made India her torso;

tail feathers: the southern ocean;
other feathers: varied rivers;
her eyes were the moon and the sun,
her crest was cosmic Mount Meru.

And making Brahma’s form appear,
she preached the doctrine of merit;
"I am Yasodharā, Hero;
I worship your feet, Eyeful One.”

I remember my former lives;
